    "infrastructure": {
      "rounds": [
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "`refresh_link` constructs `.harness/tools/bin/codex` and calls `create_dir_all`/`rename` without canonicalizing the parent and verifying it remains under `project_root`. If `.harness`, `tools`, or `bin` is a symlink to an external directory, bootstrap writes the runtime link outside the trusted repository root. Add a fail-closed trusted-root check before creating or replacing the link.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/codex_runtime.rs",
              "line": 171,
              "category": "trusted-root violation"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:3ab7762aa91935d82de587c0cc9417c00282b6b0b8bf49eb95335ca828259628",
          "at": "2026-07-18T09:37:10Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "`refresh_link` joins the repository root with `.harness/tools/bin/codex` and writes via `create_dir_all`/`rename` without verifying the resolved parent remains under the trusted project root. A symlinked `.harness`, `tools`, or `bin` directory can redirect provisioning outside the repository. Add a fail-closed trusted-root check before writing.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/codex_runtime.rs",
              "line": 171,
              "category": "trusted-root violation"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:ec015948aa50080aa7f0c057112b15ae6fbc3af0aa34151d0754884cfc553a7b",
          "at": "2026-07-18T09:42:06Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "The trusted-root checks precede `rename`, but the parent path is resolved again only before the final filesystem operation. An attacker able to replace a checked ancestor directory with a symlink in the intervening window can still redirect the atomic rename outside `trusted_root`; use directory-handle-relative operations or otherwise close this TOCTOU gap.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/codex_runtime.rs",
              "line": 201,
              "category": "trusted-root violation"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:7a98adae070673910c15157ec8f1030bf234892e1af14aac65759facd36f6289",
          "at": "2026-07-18T09:45:21Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "zero_findings",
          "findings": [],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:6d5266ae4848d5840d4054c5cf2da04c8ad19dccc5fa289deb92c69e42bcf54b",
          "at": "2026-07-18T10:01:51Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "zero_findings",
          "findings": [],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:e9120c24fc0aa2578cc55928e927fd6278bec45093259087072cf74231d7e235",
          "at": "2026-07-18T10:07:54Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "`resolve_codex_runtime` runs every candidate's `--version` probe with `Command::output()`, which has neither a deadline nor stdout/stderr limits. A broken or malicious repository-link/PATH executable can therefore hang every Codex workflow indefinitely or exhaust memory before the adapter's configured child timeout begins. Run this short probe through a bounded-output helper with a fixed deadline and map failures to `ProbeFailed`.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/codex_common.rs",
              "line": 159,
              "category": "unbounded I/O"
            },
            {
              "message": "The `npm prefix -g` fallback uses unbounded `Command::output()`. A stalled or noisy npm executable can hang bootstrap or consume unbounded memory instead of returning `NpmQueryFailed`; apply a short timeout and strict stdout/stderr caps.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/codex_runtime.rs",
              "line": 98,
              "category": "unbounded I/O"
            },
            {
              "message": "The sanitized candidate probe also uses unbounded `Command::output()`. A candidate that never exits or emits unlimited output can block/OOM bootstrap before it reaches the typed failure path. Use the bounded subprocess runner with a short probe deadline and output limit.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/codex_runtime.rs",
              "line": 139,
              "category": "unbounded I/O"
            },
            {
              "message": "Capability execution performs a second unbounded `codex --version` call solely to populate the session-log header. This happens before the provider process and outside its request timeout, so a changed or stalled executable can prevent dispatch indefinitely. Reuse the already-resolved runtime metadata or run the logging probe with bounded output and a deadline.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/capability_exec/process.rs",
              "line": 292,
              "category": "unbounded I/O"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:e9120c24fc0aa2578cc55928e927fd6278bec45093259087072cf74231d7e235",
          "at": "2026-07-18T10:18:28Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "The new ref-verifier session log writes all of `stderr_text`, which is populated by the unbounded `spawn_read_to_string` collector. A noisy or malicious Codex process can therefore grow memory and the persistent log without limit. Drain stderr with a fixed-size retained buffer and cap the session log, as the other Codex adapters do.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/ref_verify/process_runner.rs",
              "line": 458,
              "category": "unbounded I/O"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:8c0fba0511e286494ec7a2e65e3877382adc6f139304452ffa0e50a571a42828",
          "at": "2026-07-18T10:25:00Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "zero_findings",
          "findings": [],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:5e85920be11cf13996f8644691a2ef7501defb9bc1eb8d091188b66e2550c532",
          "at": "2026-07-18T10:30:06Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "`prepare_runtime_dir` validates each component with `symlink_metadata`, then performs `current.join(name)`/`create_dir` and later `canonicalize` by pathname. An attacker can replace a checked parent directory with a symlink between these operations, causing runtime creation or log/output access to escape `repo_root`; use directory-handle-relative operations (`openat`/`mkdirat`/`symlinkat`/`renameat` style) and fail closed.",
              "severity": "P0",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/capability_exec/process.rs",
              "line": 530,
              "category": "trusted-root violation"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:f1189b53054d054e5cb193caba924c53870dc988d0f54a2daaaa59ac4199cf2c",
          "at": "2026-07-18T10:55:10Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "zero_findings",
          "findings": [],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:9ccfa44bc863b5b0a2cf71cfc9f47971165e03c9f89245131676a89b41498216",
          "at": "2026-07-18T11:04:38Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "`prepare_runtime_dir` lexically removes `..` components before its handle-relative walk. A runtime path such as `repo/link/../runtime`, where `link` is a symlink, therefore bypasses symlink rejection; the Codex adapter still passes the original joined output path to the child, which can resolve it outside the trusted repository and write there. Preserve fail-closed raw-component validation before normalization (as in `normalize_path_rejecting_symlinked_components` and the `is_safe_briefing_path` traversal policy), then perform the openat walk.",
              "severity": "P0",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/capability_exec/process.rs",
              "line": 483,
              "category": "trusted-root violation"
            },
            {
              "message": "The provider-controlled output leaf is opened with blocking `RDONLY` before its file type is checked. If the child replaces the initialized file with a FIFO, `openat` waits indefinitely after the child has exited, outside the provider timeout. Open with `O_NONBLOCK` and then reject non-regular files via the handle metadata.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/capability_exec/process.rs",
              "line": 690,
              "category": "unbounded I/O"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:9ccfa44bc863b5b0a2cf71cfc9f47971165e03c9f89245131676a89b41498216",
          "at": "2026-07-18T11:12:28Z"
        },
        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "The raw traversal check still permits `ordinary/../runtime` when `ordinary` is not a symlink at validation time. That component can be replaced with a symlink immediately afterward; normalization erases it from the handle-relative walk, while Codex still receives the original path in `--output-last-message`, allowing the output write to resolve outside `repo_root`. Follow the fail-closed `is_safe_briefing_path` precedent by rejecting every `ParentDir` component before normalization, rather than relying on a raceable `symlink_metadata` snapshot.",
              "severity": "P0",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/capability_exec/process.rs",
              "line": 486,
              "category": "trusted-root violation"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:01b6d2042a645ddc013a9c7324dd4e2951caf76a27909dd6da4e8c2748b5ffe6",
          "at": "2026-07-18T11:20:20Z"
        },
